{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "a11a1001-4d7e-4b2a-9f11-6e0c1d8a4b01",
    "name": "School API — Health",
    "description": "Liveness and database ping. **Documented:** `GET /health`.\n\nNo authentication. No host check. Wrong method on `/health` is **404** (health is matched only as GET), not 405.\n\nShared environment: `environments/School-API.local.postman_environment.json`.\n\n- `{{baseUrl}}` is the **backend** (`http://127.0.0.1:5000`), not Next on `3000`.\n- Prefer `x-school-host` over `Host`. Matching lowercases and strips `:{port}`.\n- Tokens are HMAC (`payload.signature`), not JWT. Admin `{{accessToken}}` will not verify on school/campus routes (different HMAC material). School and campus share `:school-account-session`.\n- Error JSON (except health): `{ \"error\": \"<string>\" }`. No 422. Wrapper-only 500 is `{ \"error\": \"Internal server error\" }`.\n- Do not invent routes or status codes. Later batches land in the matching collection file — do not grow a monolith.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://127.0.0.1:5000"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Health",
      "description": "Liveness and database ping. No authentication. `service` is `SERVICE_TAG` or `backend-service`.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Health check",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "x-request-id",
                "value": "health-check-local",
                "description": "Optional. Echoed on the response. Generated as a UUID when omitted.",
                "disabled": true
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/health",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "health"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Returns process liveness plus a Postgres ping.\n\n**Auth:** none. Anyone can call this (compose, CI, load balancers).\n\n**Host:** ignored. No `x-school-host` required.\n\n**Side effects:** none (read-only `database.ping()`).\n\n**Status:** `200` when ping succeeds (`database: \"up\"`); `503` when ping throws (`database: \"down\"`). Both bodies share `{ ok, service, database }`.\n\n**Not used:** 400, 401, 403, 409, 422. Non-GET to this path is **not** 405 — the router only matches `GET /health`, so `POST /health` falls through to `404 { \"error\": \"Not found\" }`."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is 200 healthy or 503 unhealthy', function () {",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.be.oneOf([200, 503]);",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('health payload shape', function () {",
                  "  const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.have.property('ok').that.is.a('boolean');",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.have.property('service').that.is.a('string');",
                  "  pm.expect(body.database).to.be.oneOf(['up', 'down']);",
                  "  pm.expect(body.ok).to.eql(body.database === 'up');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "response": [
            {
              "id": "a11c1001-0001-4000-8000-000000000201",
              "name": "200 Healthy (database up)",
              "originalRequest": {
                "method": "GET",
                "header": [],
                "url": {
                  "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/health",
                  "host": [
                    "{{baseUrl}}"
                  ],
                  "path": [
                    "health"
                  ]
                }
              },
              "status": "OK",
              "code": 200,
              "_postman_previewlanguage": "json",
              "header": [
                {
                  "key": "Content-Type",
                  "value": "application/json; charset=utf-8"
                },
                {
                  "key": "x-request-id",
                  "value": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001"
                }
              ],
              "cookie": [],
              "body": "{\n  \"ok\": true,\n  \"service\": \"backend-service\",\n  \"database\": \"up\"\n}"
            },
